window.AKK_MARQUIS_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_MARQUIS_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1: System, Let's Unbind Ourselves","paragraphs":["Jiang Yunxi had died.","Then she came back to life.","But how long she could stay alive—hours, days—was still unknown.","“Pain... it hurts so much!!!”","The moment Jiang Yunxi regained even a sliver of consciousness, she was engulfed by endless agony.","They said pain came in thirteen levels. Jiang Yunxi felt that what she was experiencing had to be level fourteen.","The emperor of all emperors.","It was like a massive truck was running over her body again and again.","A fragment of her memories from before she lost consciousness resurfaced.","“So death is this painful.”","She had thought it was a final burst of awareness before death and had quietly waited for her consciousness to fade away. Yet instead, her mind grew clearer and clearer.","“What’s going on? Wasn’t I already dead? Then how...”","“Has Miss woken up yet?”","“Not yet.”","Two unfamiliar voices reached her ears, and Jiang Yunxi froze.","What was this “Miss” business?","Didn’t they call people in hell things like this ghost or that ghost?","Did ghosts need to sleep too?","The next instant, those questions seemed to trigger some kind of switch. Her head throbbed, and a flood of memories came rushing in.","Just as she was about to sort through them, an excited voice rang out in her mind.","【Host, you’re finally awake!】","【Host, I’m your System Sprite.】","Caught completely off guard by the voice, Jiang Yunxi nearly had a heart attack.","She could practically see her great-grandmother waving at her.","【Host, aren’t you surprised? Delighted?】","【I checked your memories. I know you’ve always wanted a storage space and a system!】","A System Sprite... and it was hers!","She had bonded with a system. Did that mean she wasn’t dead after all?","After reading novels for so many years, Jiang Yunxi had seen people bond with systems before—but never ghosts.","What was more, although she had not yet had time to organize the memories that had just flooded into her mind, she had caught glimpses of them.","Those memories did not belong to her.","Memories that weren’t hers, plus a system... as a veteran web-novel reader, Jiang Yunxi arrived at one conclusion.","She had transmigrated.","【System, what exactly is going on?】","【How did you bind to me?】","【Am I still alive?】","System: 【Host, you died, but then you came back to life.】","Jiang Yunxi: The art of saying nothing had truly been mastered by this thing.","Her body hurt too badly for her to waste time bantering with the system, so she impatiently urged, 【Speak plainly.】","System: 【I am speaking plainly.】","Sensing the intense fluctuations in its host’s emotions, the system did not dare keep joking and hurriedly explained.","【When you thought that, since you already had terminal cancer and only had a few days left to live anyway, you might as well trade your life for someone else’s and chose to take a bullet for a Chinese soldier, you died.】","【Completely and utterly dead.】","Jiang Yunxi: 【Then how did I come back to life?】","【Did you save me?】","The System Sprite spoke rapidly.","【To be precise, it was the Chinese soldiers who saved you.】","【It was my first time carrying out a mission. Because I was inexperienced, I went to the wrong time and space and happened to pass over your world.】","The System Sprite’s tone was full of chagrin.","【Those soldiers were desperate to save you after you were critically injured protecting their comrade. Their urgency was so strong, and their magnetic field so intense, that it affected me.","Somehow, I ended up binding with you after your body died and your soul left it.】","【The Main System discovered that I had gone to the wrong time and space—and even bound myself to the wrong host—so it came to correct the mistake.】","Yet, bound by the merit of those soldiers, the military souls and accumulated merit of the entire Huaxia armed forces were protecting you. It couldn’t forcibly sever the bond.","If it accidentally caused your soul to scatter and vanish, the System Realm would have thoroughly offended Huaxia.】","You Huaxia people are not easy to provoke. Setting aside the ancient great powers, even the hosts bound to various systems over the years would form a considerable force if they joined together.","【The Main System had no choice but to make the best of a mistake and kick both your soul and me, your system, into this time and space.】","【The Main System said that hosts can be replaced, but the time and space cannot.】","The Main System had even secretly instructed it to keep a close eye on her and make sure she didn’t get herself killed.","With all that merit and the protection of Huaxia’s military souls, if anything happened to her...","Forget this little shrimp of a system—even the Main System wouldn’t get away unscathed.","Naturally, the system didn’t dare let its host know that. It was afraid she would become reckless, knowing she had nothing to fear.","And then...","Jiang Yunxi understood.","She was glad that, in that moment, she had followed her instincts.","She had traded what little life she had left for the soldiers’ safety, never expecting such an outcome.","She had been given another chance at life, and she even had a system by her side.","She believed that, back in the modern era, the country would not treat her family unfairly.","The money they had borrowed for her treatment should be enough to pay off, and there might even be some left for her parents.","Although she had an older sister, so her parents would not be left without anyone to care for them in their old age, this at least proved that she had not been entirely useless.","This deal, Jiang Yunxi felt, was an absolute steal.","From what the system had just said, she had also picked up some information: apparently, she had powerful backing.","Even the Main System did not dare offend it, much less this little system.","Perhaps, from now on, when she did things...","Fortunately, the system could not access every thought in her mind. Otherwise...","【Why does everything hurt so much?】","【You brought me into this body—did you harm its original owner?】","【If you did harm her, who would be responsible for that?】","With merit protecting her body and all this transmigration business, Jiang Yunxi was beginning to believe in such mystical matters.","If she had harmed the original owner of this body because of her arrival, would that karma fall on the system—or on her?","Surely it could not be her fault. She had not asked the system to place her in this body.","If anyone was to blame, it should be the system—or the Main System!","【Rest assured, Host. Before you entered this body, its original owner had already died.】","【This system is a law-abiding, upstanding system. I would never do something as cruel as taking a life without regard.】","Jiang Yunxi did not feel even the slightest bit embarrassed.","Such matters had to be made clear from the start, otherwise there would be disputes later on.","【Then how did the original owner die?】","【It wasn’t revenge, was it? Am I safe now?】","【My whole body hurts. Is it because the original owner was injured, or because my soul and this body are incompatible and rejecting each other?】","【Can my soul remain in this body?】","【And what kind of system are you?】","【Please don’t tell me you’re some kind of mission system or romance-conquest system.","Let me tell you, I hate doing missions most of all, and I hate having to pursue and win over someone even more.","I’ve been single since birth. I’ve never dated, I don’t know how to date, and I definitely don’t know how to win someone over.】","【If failing missions or being unable to conquer the target means I’ll be erased, then you might as well let me die right now.】","[So I won’t have to spend every day on edge afterward, worrying that one day I might fail to complete a mission...】","Relying on what she believed was her backing, Jiang Yunxi made her stance clear right away: she didn’t want to do missions, and she didn’t want to pursue or win over anyone.","Jiang Yunxi fired off so many questions in a row that she completely stunned the system.","Hadn’t she wanted a system very badly? Why was she being so picky the moment they bonded?","Hosts these days were far too difficult to manage. She was the worst host it had ever had.","The system was deeply relieved that, before the Main System had kicked it over here, it had worried that the host might fail her missions and die, thereby offending Huaxia. So it had modified the system core.","Otherwise...","The system’s silence made Jiang Yunxi’s heart skip a beat. Could the system she’d bonded with really be a mission system—or some kind of romance-conquest system?","Then she was doomed.","She might as well give up immediately.","Having read plenty of novels, she knew those two kinds of systems were complete traps. If you failed a mission or didn’t reach the required affection level, they’d shock you with electricity or strike you with lightning.","Someone like her would be finished sooner or later.","If she was going to die sooner or later anyway, she might as well die sooner and reincarnate sooner.","Maybe, with all that accumulated merit, she could be reborn in Huaxia. Eighteen years later, she’d be a fine young woman again.","【System, let’s unbind.】"]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2: System, I Have It So Hard","paragraphs":["【System, let’s sever our bond!】","The words struck like a thunderbolt out of nowhere, crashing the System’s CPU.","The System never imagined that merely failing to respond in time would earn it a threat from its Host to sever their connection.","It hadn’t even done anything! It had only been thinking about how to answer its Host.","After all, it had originally been designed as a mission system. But then the Main System made a change, giving it the functions of two different systems.","The Main System had instructed it to let its Host enjoy gossip without risk or worry, while also finding a way to have the Host complete the original system missions without her knowing.","If a mission wasn’t completed, the punishment originally meant for the Host would instead fall on it.","Although the severity of the punishment had been reduced somewhat, it would be delayed until after this Host severed their bond, when it would be reflected in the System’s overall KPI evaluation.","When the person who was originally supposed to be punished was the Host, but the punishment had instead become its responsibility, even the System Sprite felt that it was getting a raw deal.","It felt there was nowhere it could go to seek justice.","But the Main System had said that if it hadn’t run into the wrong time-space and accidentally become bound to its current Host while gossiping, none of these troublesome matters would have happened afterward.","If it didn’t take the blame, then who would?","Even so... despite that... it still felt wronged.","It had taken such a huge risk for its Host, and not only did the Host know nothing about it, she was even threatening to sever their bond.","As a novice system binding itself to a Host for the first time, if its Host voluntarily severed the connection right after the binding, the only thing awaiting it would be being sent back for reconstruction.","Its system life was supposed to have begun with it making a name for itself in the world of systems. Instead, it was about to end before it had even started.","It kept its Host in its heart, while its Host kicked it straight into a ditch.","The System was suffering.","The System was crying pitifully.","It hurriedly sought help from the Main System, asking whether it could conceal its identity as a mission system, lest...","It was having such a hard time.","Had the Main System forgotten that it was only a novice system too? Could it really shoulder such a huge responsibility?","You’re afraid of Huaxia and don’t dare let my Host die, so you come bully me instead.","Fortunately, because of Jiang Yunxi’s special nature, the Main System had been paying close attention to the situation on their side. Its reply arrived in an instant.","After receiving the Main System’s response, the System hurriedly answered,","【Host, rest assured. This System is neither a mission system nor a strategy system. It’s merely an ordinary Gossip System.】","Jiang Yunxi felt inexplicably disdainful of the Gossip System. What use was there in binding herself to a gossip system?","Gossip was only good for passing the time!","With that time, she might as well play on her phone or read novels.","Come to think of it, where had she been transported? Were there phones and tablets here?","Jiang Yunxi had received far too many memories, and her entire body was in unbearable pain. She had no mind to sort through them just then, so she simply asked directly,","【System, you still haven’t told me what era this is, or what happened to the original owner of this body.】","【Ding—】","【The Gossip System is now officially at your service.","As for the gossip concerning this body—in other words, you, Host—would you like to hear it?】","Jiang ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍Yunxi: 【Tell me.】","How could she refuse? At the very least, this would help her figure out her current identity—and let her see whether this Gossip System was actually any good.","The System inhaled sharply: I’m very good.","The System: 【The original owner of this body was also named Jiang Yunxi.】","Jiang Yunxi: “Good. At least I won’t have to get used to another name.”","[She is currently nine years old, the Fifth Miss of the Marquis of Pingyang’s household, a daughter born to Madam Zheng, the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang’s Secondary Wife.","Because she was born after a difficult labor that left her in poor health, she had always been kept deep within the inner chambers and rarely went out.]","Jiang Yunxi: “······”","From “the Marquis of Pingyang’s household,” “daughter of a secondary wife,” and “the Heir’s Secondary Wife,” she deduced that she had transmigrated to ancient times.","Wasn’t the modern era perfectly fine? If not that, she could at least have gone to some interstellar future. Why did it have to be ancient times?","Please, let it not be the dynasty with the queue hairstyle.","Jiang Yunxi immediately interrupted the System. [System, don’t tell me I’ve transmigrated into the Qing dynasty, okay?]","[Rest assured, Host. This is not the Qing dynasty. It is a dynasty that does not exist in your history—the Yunzhao Kingdom.]","So it was an entirely fictional world.","Fictional was good. Fictional was wonderful. Fictional was absolutely fantastic.","A fictional world meant that no matter what she did here, she would not alter the history of her own timeline.","With the huge weight in her heart finally lifted, Jiang Yunxi urged, [Go on.]","[Yesterday was a holiday from the household academy. The original host was playing hide-and-seek with the maids in her family’s rear garden.","She hid behind a particular ornamental rock, never imagining that someone would sneak up behind her, knock her unconscious with a stick, and quietly throw her into the lake.]","[By the time she was rescued, she had been soaking in the water for far too long and remained unconscious.","The blow to her head had caused a blood clot in her brain. On top of that, she had been submerged for so long that her lungs became infected. With her high fever refusing to break, she eventually died.]","Jiang Yunxi frowned. [So this is an inner-household power struggle?]","What kind of inner-household power struggle was this? It was even more brutal than palace intrigue. They were using real weapons and actually killing people.","At this rate, how many people could possibly be left alive in the Marquis of Pingyang’s household?","The fact that the entire household had not already been wiped out was probably a miracle.","Jiang Yunxi asked with complete confidence,","[Was the person who did it acting on the orders of the original host’s primary wife? Or was it one of her legitimate or secondary sisters? Or perhaps one of the other concubines of the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang?]","As if she hadn’t read countless novels all these years.","Aside from those people, who else would want to get rid of the original host?","Sigh. Why had she transmigrated to ancient times? And why had she ended up as a physically frail daughter of a secondary wife?","Jiang Yunxi was deeply worried about her future.","With enemies lurking everywhere, could she, a complete novice at inner-household intrigue, survive in the marquis’s household with the help of this seemingly unreliable Gossip System?","Just listen to her title: the Fifth Miss.","In ancient times, sons and daughters were generally ranked separately. From that title alone, it was obvious that the Marquis of Pingyang’s household had quite a few children.","The struggle for power was sure to be······","[Host, you’re mistaken.]","Jiang Yunxi: “······” Why did her face feel so hot?","She had only just tried to show off her cleverness, and she had already been proven wrong.","Was there a crack in the ground she could crawl into?","Or perhaps someone could bring her a block of tofu so she could bash her head against it.","Pretending nothing had happened, she said, [You say I’m wrong, so why don’t you tell me who actually knocked out the original host and threw her into the water?]","[They must have been trying to drown her, right?]","The System replied, [It is true that someone wanted to drown her, but it wasn’t any of the people you just listed.]","[The original host could only be called unlucky. She chose the wrong place to hide while playing hide-and-seek with the maids.","There was a cave not far from the ornamental rock where she was hiding. Two people were inside playing cards.]","[The original host made a noise, startling the two of them.","They saw the original host and thought she had discovered them. To keep their secret from getting out, they decided to silence her for good.]","Jiang Yunxi was baffled. [Playing poker is just playing poker. Why would they kill someone just because they were seen?","It was only a game of poker! Was that really worth it?]","Was it worth taking the original host’s life?","As soon as the words left her mouth, Jiang Yunxi froze. She suddenly recalled the movie recaps she used to watch on TikTok.","Aside from card games, “playing poker” seemed to have another meaning.","It was all the System Sprite’s fault for being so up-to-date—she hadn’t caught on right away.","Suppressing the urge to cough awkwardly in her mind, Jiang Yunxi quickly cut off the System before it could explain.","[All right, no need to explain. I know what “playing poker” means now.]","[Just tell me who that shameless pair is.]","Now that she had taken over this body, the original host’s enemies were her enemies. She had to avenge her.","Just then, the voice of a middle-aged woman drifted over.","“Has Fifth Miss woken up yet?”","“The Old Madam has been worrying about her. She sent me over to take a look.”","The System’s voice suddenly turned shrill. [Host, it’s her.]"]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3: She's here, she's coming with rat poison","paragraphs":["Jiang Yunxi was in the middle of asking the system who had killed the original owner when a woman’s voice suddenly rang out.","At the same time, the system shrieked, 【Host, it’s her.】","Her? What did it mean, “her”?","Oh. It was talking about the pair of adulterers who had killed the original owner.","But did it mean the woman who had spoken, or the Old Madam she had mentioned?","The Old Madam... Jiang Yunxi drew in a sharp breath. Wasn’t that the original owner’s grandmother?","The woman who had committed adultery and killed the original owner couldn’t be the Old Madam—the original owner’s own grandmother, could it?","If it really was the Old Madam, how was she supposed to avenge the original owner?","Destroying her own clan outright?","Would she be struck by lightning for that?","Just as Jiang Yunxi was growing increasingly uneasy, the system spoke again.","【The nanny who just spoke is the woman from that adulterous pair. Her name is Nanny Kong, an old servant from your grandmother’s quarters.","As for the man, he’s her lover—the steward in charge of the stables in the outer residence.】","Good. There was no need to worry anymore. It wasn’t the Old Madam.","【Steward Ma was the one who knocked the original owner unconscious with a club. Nanny Kong then threw her into the lake.】","Excellent. She had found the culprits. Nanny Kong and Steward Ma, was it? Just wait until this young lady recovered. She would make sure the two of them paid with their lives for the original owner’s death.","The system spoke again.","【Host, there’s some juicy gossip about Nanny Kong. Do you want to hear it?】","Of course she did. This was the perfect opportunity to learn more about her enemy.","【Spill!】","【Nanny Kong was a young maid whom the Old Madam brought over from her maiden family. Later, the Old Madam arranged her marriage to a servant of the Pingyang Marquis’s Residence.","Her husband made a mistake once and was expelled from the residence.","Because Nanny Kong had pleaded with the Old Madam on his behalf, she escaped being implicated and continued serving at the Old Madam’s side.】","【Since the man had been dismissed for committing an offense, he had a blemish on his record and could never find a decent job. He survived by relying on Nanny Kong to support him.","But he was the sort of man who enjoyed living off a woman while still acting like her master. Whenever he was in a bad mood, he took it out on Nanny Kong. After suffering this way for years, the couple gradually grew estranged.】","Did Jiang Yunxi feel sorry for Nanny Sun?","At first, a little. But the moment she remembered that this woman had killed the original owner, all her sympathy vanished.","Instead, she felt that Nanny Kong deserved everything coming to her. Sometimes, only a villain could deal with another villain.","【Nanny Kong’s life was miserable, and Steward Ma happened to be acquainted with her husband. Knowing about her circumstances, he took advantage of her vulnerability and comforted her repeatedly. The two of them eventually began an affair.","And once they started, it continued for many years.】","【Oh, and Nanny Kong’s second son is actually Steward Ma’s child.","Fortunately, the boy resembles Nanny Kong, so no one else noticed anything.】","Impressive. Jiang Yunxi almost wanted to applaud them.","They had carried on an affair in a crowded and watchful marquis’s residence for so many years. They had even produced a child, yet no one had discovered them.","The original owner had really been unlucky. She hadn’t even uncovered their affair. Just because they suspected her, she had been...","【Host, this is bad!】","Jiang Yunxi’s heart jolted.","【Nanny Kong has come with murderous intent. The handkerchief hidden on her contains rat poison.】","【She’s afraid you’ll wake up and expose her affair with Steward Ma. She’s here to finish the job and silence you for good!】","Damn it! This woman was ruthless. She had actually come back to deliver a second blow!","What was wrong with people in ancient times? Did human life really mean so little to them?","Jiang Yunxi tried to call for help, only to discover that this body seemed to be beyond her control. She couldn’t even open her eyes, let alone get up and cry for help.","Sensing her struggle, the system hurriedly explained:","【Host, this body currently has pneumonia and a high fever. On top of that, your soul has only just entered it and hasn’t adapted yet, so you won’t be able to wake up for a while.】","Jiang Yunxi panicked.","【Then what do we do? Hurry up and save me!","I’m lying here completely helpless. Isn’t that just making it convenient for her to poison me?】","【You and I are in the same boat now. If one of us prospers, we both prosper; if one of us suffers, we both suffer. You can’t just stand by and watch me die.】","Although she had threatened the system earlier, saying that if it made her complete missions and pursue men, she would rather die sooner, Jiang Yunxi still didn’t want to die now that the moment had actually arrived.","After all, a bad life was still better than no life.","And besides, she would be dying at the hands of her enemy.","If she let her enemy have her way, she was afraid she wouldn’t be able to rest in peace—even the lid of her coffin might not stay shut.","【Host, I can’t do anything right now.","I can only speak inside your mind. It’s not as if I can call for help on your behalf.】","Jiang Yunxi was furious. What a useless system! She had known it couldn’t be relied on.","With such a worthless system, how was she supposed to survive in this ancient world, where she had been thrown straight into a life-or-death crisis?","【System, after I die, I’m going to file a complaint. I’ll report your entire system realm for treating human lives as worthless.","You only know how to bind yourselves to hosts. You don’t take responsibility for anything else. You’re all about killing without bothering to bury the dead.】","The system’s CPU nearly began smoking.","What should it do? Its host was about to die, and it was unlikely to complete the main system’s mission.","The system realm was certain to offend Huaxia, and it would inevitably be sent back for reprogramming as well.","The system glanced over its administrative interface. It was so familiar, yet so strange. It had to memorize every detail. After this, it might never see them again.","Suddenly, it spotted two lines of data, and its eyes lit up.","【Ding! Host successfully consumed the original owner’s gossip. Gossip Points +300.】","【Ding! Host successfully consumed Nanny Kong’s gossip. Gossip Points +100.】","Jiang Yunxi, who was preoccupied with saving her own life, barely paid attention when she heard the two notifications.","【Host, there’s a way!","I have a system shop. You can use 100 Gossip Points to unlock it, then buy an Antidote to All Poisons.","That way, even if she poisons you, you won’t have to worry.】","At that moment, the system’s voice sounded like the most beautiful, wonderful music in the world to Jiang Yunxi.","【Unlock it, unlock it! Do it now!】","【Buy it, buy it! Get it immediately!】","【All right, Host. I’ll unlock the system shop and purchase the Antidote to All Poisons right away.】","It felt as though a century had passed. In reality, less than five seconds later, the system spoke hesitantly.","【Host, the purchase failed. You don’t have enough Gossip Points.】","What a useless system!","Had it been deceiving her just now?","Didn’t it know the prices of the items in its own shop?","【How many points are we short?","Can’t you give me a discount, or let me buy it on credit?】","【Discounts and credit both require approval from the main system.】","More procedures. Always more procedures. At that moment, Jiang Yunxi hated those procedures with every fiber of her being.","【Then hurry up and get approval.】","Although she was speaking only in her mind, Jiang Yunxi felt as if she had shouted herself hoarse.","While Jiang Yunxi and the system were discussing Nanny Kong’s secrets and desperately trying to find a way to save her life, Nanny Kong had already finished speaking with the maids and matrons in Jiang Yunxi’s courtyard. She was now walking step by step toward Jiang Yunxi, who lay on the bed.","Nanny Kong’s footsteps were steady. Each step landed on the gray brick floor with a soft click-click, like someone striking Jiang Yunxi’s heart with a hammer and making her nerves draw taut.","To her ears, that sound was no different from the approach of the Grim Reaper.","She was coming. She was coming, carrying rat poison with her.","At that moment, Jiang Yunxi’s soul, which was already poorly attuned to the body, seemed ready to leave it again.","She struggled desperately to open her eyes and call for help, but her body felt as though it had been nailed to the bed. She couldn’t move a muscle, and not even the faintest sound could escape her throat.","All she could do was listen as the footsteps drew closer and closer, becoming clearer with every step, until they finally stopped beside her bed.","“Poor Fifth Miss!”","Jiang Yunxi felt someone gently stroking her face. The touch was incredibly light, yet to her it felt as heavy as a thousand jun.","That ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍voice belonged to Nanny Kong.","Clearly, it was Nanny Kong who was touching her.","Was the next step going to be pressing a handkerchief smeared with rat poison over her face...?","“How could you have fallen into the lake so carelessly and nearly drowned yourself like this?”","“Nanny, just hearing about it makes my heart feel as though it’s being torn apart. I can only imagine how the Old Madam must feel.”","Jiang Yunxi thought, “Aaahhh... That Kong woman, you poisonous old hag! Stop putting on such a shameless act. Wasn’t it you and your lover who attacked me from behind, knocked me unconscious, and threw me into the lake, leaving me in this state?”","Outside the room, a woman staggered on her feet and nearly fell."]}]);
